  "id": "image",
  "name": "Image",
  "kind": "struct",
  "declaration": "public struct Image: _PrimitiveView",
  "abstract": "Bitmap image primitive backed by an owned CPU asset or a registered GPU texture.",
  "discussion": [
   "File images retain their decoded asset with the draw list. NativeRHI\nrenderers upload it on first use. Hosts can also supply a manually registered\n`TextureID`. Layout uses the explicit logical `width` and `height`.",
   "`tint` multiplies the sampled RGBA. Pass `.white` (default) for an\nuntouched bitmap, or any other color to recolour an opaque shape (acts as\na multiplicative tint, matching the shader's `color * texture` path)."
