   {
    "name": "Image",
    "kind": "init",
    "declaration": "init(file path: String, width: Float, height: Float, tint: Color = .white, contentMode: ContentMode = .stretch, renderingMode: RenderingMode = .color)",
    "abstract": "Convenience initializer that loads `path` through the registry in `ImageAssetRegistryHolder.current`, then renders the resulting `TextureID` at the requested size.",
    "discussion": [
     "First call decodes and retains CPU pixels; GPU upload belongs to the\nconsuming renderer. Subsequent calls hit the in-memory\ncache. Vector formats (SVG/PDF) are rasterised at the requested\npixel dimensions so passing different sizes produces different\ncrisp textures.",
     "A registry provides shared caching; decoding works without one.\nIf decoding fails, the primitive degrades to\n`TextureID.none` (a tinted blank quad of the requested size)."
    ]
