 {
  "id": "ui-icons",
  "name": "UIIcons",
  "kind": "enum",
  "declaration": "public enum UIIcons",
  "abstract": "The bundled icon set.",
  "discussion": [
   "Every asset is authored on a 24x24 grid and drawn through\n`renderingMode: .alphaMask`, so the alpha channel becomes coverage and\nthe foreground color becomes the fill. Icons therefore follow theme\ntokens instead of their authored colors, and one asset serves every\ndensity.",
   "Glyphs that are routinely drawn at 8-14px (`chevron-*`, `check`, `x`,\n`plus`, `minus`) are authored with a heavier stroke so they stay\nlegible when scaled down; everything else uses the 2.0 default.",
   "```swift\nIcon(UIIcons.Navigation.chevronDown, size: 12, color: .onSurfaceMuted)\nIcon(UIIcons.Status.starFill, size: 16, color: .warning)\n```"
  ],
